  <title>Draft job sheets</title>

  <p>The <gui>Draft Job Sheets</gui> button of the main window lists every
  <link xref="job_sheet">job sheet</link> that is neither invoiced nor
  completed. Double click a job to see its products below.</p>

  <terms>
    <item><title><gui>Post Job to Invoice</gui></title>
    <p>Closes the job and adds its products to the customer's draft invoice,
    at the customer's prices, taxed with their <link xref="invoice#tax">tax
    exemption</link>. If the customer already has a draft invoice, you
    are asked whether to add them to it; the lines already on it keep their
    prices. The job leaves the <link xref="time_clock">time
    clock</link>.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Post Job as Completed</gui></title>
    <p>Closes the job without invoicing anything. It leaves the time clock
    too.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Open in Job Sheet window</gui></title>
    <p>Opens the job to change it.</p></item>
  </terms>

  <p>To move a job to another customer, right click it, choose <gui>Move job
  to contact</gui>, pick the contact and click <gui>Move</gui>.</p>

</page>
